What it is

Implicit wait tells Appium:

“Whenever you try to find an element, wait up to X seconds before saying it is not found.”

It is a global wait applied to all elements.

💻 Example
driver.manage().timeouts().implicitlyWait(Duration.ofSeconds(10));
⚙️ How it works

If element is not found immediately:

Appium keeps trying until timeout (e.g., 10 seconds)
Then throws NoSuchElementException

// Step 1: Wait for login button
WebElement login = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(
        By.id("com.app:id/login_button")
    )
);

// Step 2: Click login
login.click();

// Step 3: Wait for dashboard
wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(
        By.id("com.app:id/dashboard")
    )
);

Wait<WebDriver> wait = new FluentWait<>(driver)
    .withTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(20))
    .pollingEvery(Duration.ofSeconds(3))
    .ignoring(NoSuchElementException.class);

WebElement login = wait.until(driver ->
    driver.findElement(By.id("com.app:id/login_button"))
);

login.click();

